  "resultText": "Check-in now returns 422 with `OverdueBalanceError` when the visitor has an open invoice older than 30 days. `npm test` passes (34 unit tests and 5 e2e tests), and lint and typecheck are clean.\n\n- **Cross-context query:** Front-desk shouldn't import Billing internals, so I added a small contract, `OverdueBalanceQuery`, in `src/contracts/billing.queries.ts`. Billing implements it through `InvoicingService`, and `FrontDeskModule` now imports `BillingModule`.\n- **Overdue rule:** `Invoice.isOverdue(now)` in `invoice.ts` returns true for an open invoice issued more than 30 days before `now`. An invoice exactly 30 days old is not overdue.\n- **Check-in:** `VisitsService.checkIn` asks the query before changing the visit. If the answer is yes, it throws `OverdueBalanceError` (added to `visit.errors.ts`). The visit stays `EXPECTED` and no `VisitorCheckedIn` event goes out. The existing error filter turns it into the 422 response.\n- **Tests:** I added tests for the 30-day boundary on the invoice. I added tests for the billing check, including that other payers' invoices are ignored. A new `visits.service.spec.ts` covers the check-in. A new e2e case shows a no-show fee invoice blocking a later check-in more than 30 days on, while another visitor still checks in.\n\nBecause the overdue check runs first, an overdue visitor whose visit is cancelled or already checked in gets `OverdueBalanceError` rather than the existing state error. Say if you'd rather the state errors win.",
